{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Debugging RCA for CI run 33540993369: all three Linux pytest matrix failures were the same deterministic assertion in `tests/unit/test_release_workflow_pins.py::test_all_uses_are_full_sha_pinned`. Existing guard enforced `@<40-hex-sha>` for every `uses:` in release.yml, which is correct for remote actions but wrong for repo-local composite actions because a relative `uses: ./...` is pinned by the reviewed commit itself. Working example/context: repo already uses relative local action `./.github/actions/docs-gates`; new uv guard covers local setup action contents/checksums. Fix: skip relative `./` uses in the remote-action SHA guard and add `test_repo_local_actions_are_not_sha_pinned` asserting release.yml uses the local setup action. Validation: `pytest tests/unit/test_release_workflow_pins.py::test_all_uses_are_full_sha_pinned tests/unit/test_release_workflow_pins.py::test_repo_local_actions_are_not_sha_pinned tests/unit/test_uv_pin_guard.py -q` => 19 passed; `make lint` => passed."},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1788288236308767311,"uuid":"e7f0e6f1-c811-46ef-9231-591781e3186a"}